From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Mills <travismills82@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 18:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ors: fix restore action label and CLI usage

The OpenRecoveryScript restore path asks the GUI to resolve a string named
`restore`, but the bundled language files expose `restore_hdr` and
`restoring`. This produces an otherwise harmless but user-visible resource
error at the start of every command-line restore.

The command-line help also documents the restore arguments in the opposite
order from the parser. A restore command is `restore <backup-folder> [SDCRBAEM]`;
the folder must come first so the parser can select the requested partitions
from it.

Use the existing translated restore header and document the actual argument
order.
---
 openrecoveryscript.cpp | 2 +-
 orscmd/orscmd.cpp      | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/openrecoveryscript.cpp b/openrecoveryscript.cpp
index 00000000..00000000 100644
--- a/openrecoveryscript.cpp
+++ b/openrecoveryscript.cpp
@@ -208 +208 @@ int OpenRecoveryScript::run_script_file(void) {
-				DataManager::SetValue("tw_action_text2", gui_parse_text("{@restore}"));
+				DataManager::SetValue("tw_action_text2", gui_parse_text("{@restore_hdr}"));
diff --git a/orscmd/orscmd.cpp b/orscmd/orscmd.cpp
index 00000000..00000000 100644
--- a/orscmd/orscmd.cpp
+++ b/orscmd/orscmd.cpp
@@ -44 +44 @@ void print_usage(void) {
-	printf("  restore <SDCRBAEM> [backupname]\n");
+	printf("  restore <backupname> [SDCRBAEM]\n");
